{"authored" [{"question" "q-97303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨b,a⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨a,b⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $i⟨a,b⟩=⟨-ia,b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is false. A complex  inner product is linear  in the first argument,  so we have \n\n$$\n⟨-ia,b⟩=-i⟨a,b⟩\\ne i⟨a,b⟩,\n$$\n\nin general.\n\n- Statement III is true. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$  $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe81600b8b96eef35cd9250940e7d4a6ae13488815ff948751be80edf21eec0b" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=2-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨b,c⟩=1+2\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨2a,c⟩+⟨3b,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨b,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2(\\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2(2+\\text{i})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4+2\\text{i}+3+6\\text{i} \\\\  & =7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe81600b8b96eef35cd9250940e7d4a6ae13488815ff948751be80edf21eec0b" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "7+4\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "7+8\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.js