on" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨2a-b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,c⟩=8+\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,b⟩=4-5\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2a-b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨2a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩ & =2⟨a,c⟩-\\overset{―}{⟨c,b}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨a,c⟩$ and $⟨c,b⟩:$    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩-\\overset{―}{⟨c,b}⟩ & =2(8+\\text{i})-(\\overset{―}{4-5\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =2(8+\\text{i})-(4+5\\text{i}) \\\\  & =16+2\\text{i}-4-5\\text{i} \\\\  & =12-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe81600b8b96eef35cd9250940e7d4a6ae13488815ff948751be80edf21eec0b" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5+6\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "10+8\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "12-3\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4-\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6+8\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12-3\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/state.json" "file_sha256" "671890b0211b06620cb6e3464932abf4c11db576f0b554a6a49c898b4dd9c32f" "basis" 1843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,0⟩=0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $2⟨a,b⟩=⟨a,-2b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e7521b716cdccd6db272fe51f63c62a5755cf7b80f7b9c53c977f25cdd9cbf8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the antilinearity in the second argument we have that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,0⟩ & =⟨a,0\\cdot 0⟩=\\overset{―}{0}⟨a,0⟩=0⟨a,0⟩=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,-2b⟩=\\overset{―}{(-2)}⟨a,b⟩=-2⟨a,b⟩\\ne 2⟨a,b⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e7521b716cdccd6db272fe51f63c62a5755cf7b80f7b9c53c977f25cdd9cbf8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "82795b2335fa4e93428dcb8f3fd4318fb308a7d85fe4917b9dd19eb0df0f46e8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e7521b716cdccd6db272fe51f63c62a5755cf7b80f7b9c53c977f25cdd9cbf8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e7521b716cdccd6db272fe51f63c62a5755cf7b80f7b9c53c977f25cdd9cbf8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e7521b716cdccd6db272fe51f63c62a5755cf7b80f7b9c53c977f25cdd9cbf8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e7521b716cdccd6db272fe51f63c62a5755cf7b80f7b9c53c977f25cdd9cbf8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e7521b716cdccd6db272fe51f63c62a5755cf7b80f7b9c53c977f25cdd9cbf8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e7521b716cdccd6db272fe51f63c62a5755cf7b80f7b9c53c977f25cdd9cbf8" "basis" 2043 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-97167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨2a-b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,c⟩=8+\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,b⟩=4-5\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2a-b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨2a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩ & =2⟨a,c⟩-\\overset{―}{⟨c,b}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨a,c⟩$ and $⟨c,b⟩:$    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩-\\overset{―}{⟨c,b}⟩ & =2(8+\\text{i})-(\\overset{―}{4-5\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =2(8+\\text{i})-(4+5\\text{i}) \\\\  & =16+2\\text{i}-4-5\\text{i} \\\\  & =12-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c85a7049ebf13f24aced7e0921c06a01dd7d94d8f90ecfa05f88253d382e440"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5+6\\text{i}"] ["math" "10+8\\text{i}"] ["math" "12-3\\text{i}"] ["math" "4-\\text{i}"] ["math" "6+8\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12-3\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨b,a⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨a,b⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $i⟨a,b⟩=⟨-ia,b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is false. A complex  inner product is linear  in the first argument,  so we have \n\n$$\n⟨-ia,b⟩=-i⟨a,b⟩\\ne i⟨a,b⟩,\n$$\n\nin general.\n\n- Statement III is true. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$  $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c85a7049ebf13f24aced7e0921c06a01dd7d94d8f90ecfa05f88253d382e440"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,0⟩=0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $2⟨a,b⟩=⟨a,-2b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the antilinearity in the second argument we have that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,0⟩ & =⟨a,0\\cdot 0⟩=\\overset{―}{0}⟨a,0⟩=0⟨a,0⟩=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,-2b⟩=\\overset{―}{(-2)}⟨a,b⟩=-2⟨a,b⟩\\ne 2⟨a,b⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c85a7049ebf13f24aced7e0921c06a01dd7d94d8f90ecfa05f88253d382e440"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in R$\n- $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. For any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\overset{―}{\\alpha }=\\alpha .$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $a=0,$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c85a7049ebf13f24aced7e0921c06a01dd7d94d8f90ecfa05f88253d382e440"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=2-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨b,c⟩=1+2\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨2a,c⟩+⟨3b,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨b,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2(\\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2(2+\\text{i})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4+2\\text{i}+3+6\\text{i} \\\\  & =7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c85a7049ebf13f24aced7e0921c06a01dd7d94d8f90ecfa05f88253d382e440"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "7+4\\text{i}"] ["math" "7+8\\text{i}"] ["math" "7-4\\text{i}"] ["math" "8+7\\text{i}"] ["math" "8+\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"} {"question" "q-141161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7+8\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "56769178e0d5e359edf5bed74cb10baa3747d176028ce55f3a68509ac9243784"}] "usage" {"q-97305" [] "q-141161" [] "q-97167" [] "q-97303" []} "basis" 2541 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186133275 17592186133276 17592186133277 17592186133278 17592186133279 17592186334268 17592186334269 17592186334270 17592186334271 17592186334272 17592186334310 17592186334311 17592186334312 17592186334313 17592186334314 17592186334317 17592186334318 17592186334319 17592186334320 17592186334321] "immutable_fields" [[17592186133274 :answer-field/correct] [17592186133274 :answer-field/id] [17592186133274 :answer-field/key] [17592186133274 :answer-field/type] [17592186334267 :answer-field/correct] [17592186334267 :answer-field/id] [17592186334267 :answer-field/key] [17592186334267 :answer-field/type] [17592186334309 :answer-field/correct] [17592186334309 :answer-field/id] [17592186334309 :answer-field/key] [17592186334309 :answer-field/type] [17592186334316 :answer-field/correct] [17592186334316 :answer-field/id] [17592186334316 :answer-field/key] [17592186334316 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
